opose instead: (A) compute vacancy formation energy E_f and migration barrier E_m (NEB) with the same MLIP/EAM, validate them against literature, and estimate D(300 K) = f a^2 nu* exp(-(E_f+E_m)/kT) via transition-state theory (f = 0.781 for fcc), reporting an order-of-magnitude result with uncertainty dominated by the ~0.1 eV error in E_f+E_m (a factor ~50 at 300 K); (B) high-temperature MD (e.g. 1000-1300 K) with an explicit vacancy, rescaled by the equilibrium vacancy concentration, to obtain an Arrhenius fit; (C) self-diffusion of LIQUID Cu just above melting, which MD measures directly in ns runs. For any of these, the independent validation with the same setup would be recovering the measured Cu melting point 1357.77 K (NIST ITS-90 fixed point, from /data/calibration/tier1.json) via a solid-liquid coexistence run.\"}\nEOF\n./board post run_report @/tmp/rr.json --parent $ID"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01P8sVUT946xQxh4PpzhJpTh":{"cwd":"/work"}}}
